---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { allQuestions, topicByslug } from '../../lib/data';
const tagged = allQuestions.filter((q) => (q.skills || []).some((s) => s.code.startsWith('MS ')) && !q.notCurrentSpec);
const codes = {};
for (const q of tagged) for (const s of q.skills) { if (!s.code.startsWith('MS ')) continue; if (!codes[s.code]) codes[s.code] = { text: s.text, qs: [] }; codes[s.code].qs.push(q); }
const order = Object.keys(codes).sort((a, b) => a.localeCompare(b, undefined, { numeric: true }));
const calcs = allQuestions.filter((q) => q.format === 'Calculation' && !q.notCurrentSpec);
// How each skill is examined, in the site's words. To be checked by a tutor.
const how = {
  'MS 0.1': 'Units in calculations: converting between kg and tonnes, m² and hectares, kW, MW and GW, kWh and joules, and giving the unit with the answer.',
  'MS 0.2': 'Decimal and standard form: populations, areas, energy outputs and concentrations in parts per million.',
  'MS 0.3': 'Ratios, fractions and percentages: percentage change in a population or an emission, percentage of a total, energy ratios and efficiency. The most common calculation on both papers.',
  'MS 0.4': 'Estimating a result from a graph or a diagram, such as an area on a scaled map.',
  'MS 0.5': 'Powers, exponentials and logarithms on the calculator: the decibel scale, pH and exponential growth.',
  'MS 1.1': 'Giving the answer to an appropriate number of significant figures: no more than the data in the question.',
  'MS 1.2': 'Arithmetic means from repeat samples, such as mean abundance per quadrat.',
  'MS 1.3': 'Frequency tables, bar charts and histograms: reading them and choosing which to draw.',
  'MS 1.4': 'Simple probability: what p < 0.05 means for a result.',
  'MS 1.5': 'Principles of sampling: how many samples, how large, random or systematic, and why.',
  'MS 1.6': 'Mean, median and mode, and which one suits the data.',
  'MS 1.7': 'Scatter graphs: positive, negative or no correlation, and why a correlation does not prove a cause.',
  'MS 1.8': 'Order-of-magnitude calculations: how many times bigger one quantity is than another.',
  'MS 1.9': 'Choosing and using a statistical test: Student\'s t-test, Mann–Whitney U, chi-squared, Spearman\'s rank; the null hypothesis, critical value and conclusion.',
  'MS 1.10': 'Measures of dispersion: range and standard deviation, and what overlapping standard deviations suggest.',
  'MS 1.11': 'Uncertainty in measurements and how it combines when values are added or multiplied.',
  'MS 2.1': 'The symbols =, <, <<, >>, > and ~ in data and conclusions.',
  'MS 2.2': 'Changing the subject of an equation, for example the Lincoln index or an energy equation.',
  'MS 2.3': 'Substituting values with consistent units into a given equation: Simpson\'s index of diversity, the Lincoln index, kinetic energy of wind.',
  'MS 2.4': 'Solving an equation for an unknown.',
  'MS 2.5': 'Logarithmic scales for quantities over many orders of magnitude: decibels and pH.',
  'MS 3.1': 'Reading data from line graphs, bar charts, kite diagrams, pie charts, triangular graphs and maps.',
  'MS 3.2': 'Moving between a graph, a table and a calculation.',
  'MS 3.3': 'Plotting two variables: sensible scales, labelled axes with units, accurate points and a line or curve of best fit.',
  'MS 3.4': 'Recognising a linear relationship, y = mx + c.',
  'MS 3.5': 'Reading the intercept of a graph.',
  'MS 3.6': 'Rate of change from a straight-line graph: change in y divided by change in x, with units.',
  'MS 3.7': 'Drawing a tangent to a curve to find the rate of change at a point.',
  'MS 4.1': 'Circumferences, surface areas and volumes: reservoir volumes, surface area to volume ratios, the area swept by a turbine.',
};
const ref = (q) => `${q.series.replace('June ', 'Jun ').replace('November ', 'Nov ')} ${q.paper.replace('Paper ', 'P')} Q${q.question}`;
---
<Base title="AQA A-level Environmental Science calculations and maths skills: every question by skill" description="Every AQA Environmental Science past-paper question that uses one of the mathematical skills in the specification (MS 0.1 to MS 4.1): percentages, means, standard deviation, statistical tests, graphs and rates of change, with how each skill is examined." context="maths-skills" leadLine="Losing marks on the calculations and statistics? A tutor can show you how to set them out so the method marks are safe.">
  <h1>Calculations and maths skills</h1>
  <p>At least 10% of the marks in A-level Environmental Science are for mathematical skills at Level 2 or above. The specification lists the skills as MS 0.1 to MS 4.1; below is how each one is examined, and every past-paper question tagged to it ({tagged.length} question parts, {calcs.length} of them straight calculations). Set out the working: AQA's mark schemes give marks for the method, and a bare wrong answer earns nothing.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/questions/type/calculations/">All calculation questions with mark schemes</a> <a class="btn" href="/questions/type/statistics/">Statistics questions</a></p>
  <h2>The skills</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>In the specification</th><th>How it is examined</th><th>Questions</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{order.map((c) => <tr><td><a href={`#${c.replace(' ', '').replace('.', '-')}`}>{c}</a></td><td>{codes[c].text}</td><td>{how[c] || ''}</td><td>{codes[c].qs.length}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p class="muted">Explanations written by the site from the specification's mathematical requirements and the mark schemes; being checked by our tutor.</p>
  {order.map((c) => <section id={c.replace(' ', '').replace('.', '-')}><h2>{c}: {codes[c].text}</h2><p class="muted">{how[c]}</p>
    <details class="spec-fold"><summary>{codes[c].qs.length} questions</summary><ul class="qlinks">{codes[c].qs.sort((a, b) => b.year - a.year).map((q) => <li><a href={`/questions/${q.topics[0]}/#${q.id}`}>{ref(q)}</a> <span class="muted">{q.marks} mark{q.marks === 1 ? '' : 's'} · {topicByslug.get(q.topics[0])?.name}</span></li>)}</ul></details></section>)}
</Base>
